Compile is clean (one non-blocking, physically correct connectivity note: the soil and pot shell are separate mesh shells with different materials). Final geometry:

- **Pot (root)**: genuinely hollow lathed concrete vessel — 8–14 mm wall, thicker solid base, subtly tapered sides, open mouth with rim; a separate potting-soil disc sits just below the rim.
- **Articulation**: `pot_to_plant_stem` revolute at the soil line (±0.07 rad) — the whole plant can sway.
- **Five leaf sprays** (`leaf_spray_0…4`), each a thin curved side stem with four pointed, cupped, thickness-modelled leaves, each mounted to the main stem on its own revolute swing joint (±0.14 rad) about the horizontal axis perpendicular to its stem.
- **Main stem** carries five leaves sparsely branching outward, giving a dense, layered crown (crown ≈ 1.4× pot diameter, pot 14 cm dia × 15 cm tall, full plant ~30 cm) with dark/light green variegation, matching the reference.
- Intentional local overlaps (stem planted into soil, dense foliage interleaving) are declared with scoped allowances and paired with contact/seating/overlap proof checks; `fit_to_box` enforces the exact scale and placement.

